# Insert sets (a viewer on askNK's video): a file with several objects is a set; its picker shows a thumbnail per
# item; [ and ] step through it while inserting. kitbash_set.glb: Stud (8 triangles), Wedge (4); X symmetry is on.
run new_sphere subdivisions=4
key f
remember triangles base
choose_file insert_set data/kitbash_set.glb
wait 0.1
expect_status Insert Stud (1 of 2)
wait_idle
shot insert_set_picker

# Item 0, then ] to item 1: each drag inserts the item chosen (with its mirrored copy).
stroke 0.8 0.45 0.86 0.45
expect_status 2 Studs (mirrored)
expect_value triangles == $base+16
key ]
expect_status Insert Wedge (2 of 2)
stroke 0.8 0.55 0.86 0.55
expect_status 2 Wedges (mirrored)
expect_value triangles == $base+24
shot insert_set_items

# ] wraps around, [ steps back; a click on a tile picks it.
key ]
expect_status Insert Stud (1 of 2)
key [
expect_status Insert Wedge (2 of 2)
click "##insertset0"
expect_status Insert Stud (1 of 2)
key ]
expect_status Insert Wedge (2 of 2)
key ctrl+z
expect_value triangles == $base+16
key escape
expect_status Insert off
